.Dd September 19, 2025
.Dt BASSE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm basse
.Nd blazingly fast Base64 encoder and decoder
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl w | \-wrap Ar column
.Ar infile
.Nm
.Fl d | \-decode
.Op Fl o | \-output Ar outfile
.Ar infile
.Nm
.Fl h | \-help
.Nm
.Fl V | \-version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility encodes or decodes a binary file from and to ASCII according to the
rules of Base64, as specified by RFC 4648, allowing binary data to be
transmitted over ASCII-only protocols like e\-mail. The
.Nm
utility utilizes SIMD capabilities of the processor, if available, for
fast encoding and decoding.
.Pp
If
.Ar infile
is not specified, or if
.Ar infile
is
.Ql \- ,
.Nm
reads standard input.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl V , Fl \-version
Print version information and exit.
.It Fl d , Fl \-decode
Treat
.Ar infile
or standard input as Base64 data and decode it.
.It Fl h , Fl \-help
Print a quick help and exit.
.It Fl o , Fl \-output Ar outfile
Write encoded or decoded data to
.Ar outfile
instead of standard output.
.It Fl w , Fl \-wrap Ar column
If
.Ar column
is positive, wrap encoded output after
.Ar column .
If
.Ar column
is zero or negative, do not wrap encoded output. By default,
.Nm
wraps after 76 columns. Ignored if the
.Fl d
flag is used.
.El
.Sh IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
The
.Fl i
or
.Fl \-ignore\-garbage
flag, available in GNU coreutils, is not recognized by
.Nm .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Lk "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4648" "RFC 4648" .
.Rs
